id: shadow-dragon-genes
name: Shadow Dragon Genes
order: 16
category: body
importance: secondary
description: >
  Comprised of the negative energy of the Shadow Dragons, you share some of their ability to warp reality.
text: >
  Shadow Dragon Genes [Morale] (Body): Comprised of the negative energy of the Shadow Dragons, you share some of their ability to warp reality.
  (1)-[Passive]: Increase your Racial Life Modifier by 2.
  (2)-[Triggered/Start of Turn]: You may reduce your Life Points by up to 8(bT) to regain an equal amount of Ki Points.
  (3)-[Triggered]: If you gain an Adaptation Point, regain 1(bT) Ki Points.
  (4)-[Triggered]: If an Opponent who is not at Long Range scores a Botch Result, you may spend an Adaptation Point to inflict the Impaired Combat Condition on that Opponent until the start of their next turn.
  (5)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you reduce your Life Points by 4(bT) or more through the second effects of Dragon Genes, gain an Adaptation Point.
  (6)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: If you reduce your Life Points by 8(bT) or more through the second effects of Dragon Genes, gain 2 Adaptation Points.
---

[passive]
# [Morale]: its Racial Saving Throw Bonus.
allow save.racial.morale;
# (1)
racialLifeModifier += 2;
# (4) An Opponent not at Long Range scoring a Botch on an attack's card, with an Adaptation Point: asked - Impaired till the start of
# their next turn (chat.mjs shadowGenesImpair).
allow shadowDragonGenes.impair;
# (6) 8(bT) or more traded through (2): asked, once an Encounter - no Triggered/Automatic button, the use being the Encounter's one (the
# user's): 2 Adaptation Points (chat.mjs shadowGenesTrade).
allow shadowDragonGenes.eight;

# (2) Your turn begins: how much Life, up to 8(bT), asked - as much Ki (chat.mjs shadowGenesTrade); then its Moment, what was traded
# (life-for-ki). It spends Life Points - a resource: no Triggered/Automatic button, ticked on the turn's card (the user's).
[triggered/start-of-turn, chosen, effect 2]
shadowGenesTrade();

# (3) An Adaptation Point gained. Automatic by default, its Triggered/Automatic button.
[triggered/adaptation-gained, effect 3]
ki.value += 1(bT);

# (5) What (2) traded. Automatic by default, its Triggered/Automatic button.
[triggered/life-for-ki, 1/round, effect 5]
requires lostAtLeastBT(4);
adaptation.stacks += 1;
